From 40be6dbf9dc5ba424a435ba5f46214d3f0a94f8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:35:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [AGS] Gate Glad::Glad (OpenGL loader) out for DOS

The AGS_OPENGLES2 else() branch linked Glad::Glad unconditionally for
every non-GLES2 platform, including DOS. DOS has no hardware-renderer
path at all -- window-surface presentation only (patches/ags/0017) --
so it is excluded directly. No CMake-level AGS_HAS_OPENGL variable
exists to gate on generically (confirmed: platform.h's AGS_HAS_OPENGL
is a C-preprocessor-only macro, not visible to CMake); every other
platform this file supports wants OpenGL today, so a targeted `NOT DOS`
exclusion is the minimal, honest fix rather than introducing a new
CMake-level mirror of that macro for one platform.
---
 Engine/CMakeLists.txt | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Engine/CMakeLists.txt b/Engine/CMakeLists.txt
index 468f2c9cf..b6a3f897c 100644
--- a/Engine/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Engine/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -565,7 +565,14 @@ endif()
 
 if (AGS_OPENGLES2)
     target_link_libraries(engine PUBLIC EGL GLESv2 Glad::GladGLES2)
-else()
+elseif (NOT DOS)
+    # DOS-PORT: every other platform this file supports wants desktop
+    # OpenGL (there is no separate AGS_HAS_OPENGL CMake variable to gate
+    # on -- platform.h's own AGS_HAS_OPENGL macro is a C-preprocessor-only
+    # concept, not visible here). DOS has no hardware-renderer path at
+    # all (window-surface presentation only, patches/ags/0017), so it is
+    # excluded directly rather than introducing a CMake-level mirror of
+    # platform.h's macro for a single platform.
     target_link_libraries(engine PUBLIC Glad::Glad)
 endif (AGS_OPENGLES2)
 
